WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.580
- You can grow mint in the ground

00:00:01.580 --> 00:00:04.270
but this is where we have
our disclaimer for mint.

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:07.600
Mint is a very aggressively growing plant.

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:10.290
That means that where you plant mint

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:13.610
it will expand and it will
pop up all over your garden.

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:16.060
So my tip for you in growing mint

00:00:16.060 --> 00:00:21.060
is to either grow it in a pot
or grow it in a raised bed.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:25.990
If you don't want to dedicate
a whole raised bed to mint

00:00:25.990 --> 00:00:30.990
you can actually bury a pot in the soil

00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:34.290
and that will help keep mint in this area.

00:00:34.290 --> 00:00:35.690
We're gonna take your pot

00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:37.600
and your pot can be as big as you want

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:39.730
if you want a bigger section of mint.

00:00:39.730 --> 00:00:42.310
If it's at soil level
the runners would expand

00:00:42.310 --> 00:00:43.310
right across the soil.

00:00:43.310 --> 00:00:46.150
So you wanna leave it high
up, keeping your mint in check

00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:47.525
if you don't want it to take over.

00:00:47.525 --> 00:00:50.108
(upbeat music)

